<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mem de Sá</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1500–<a href="/years/1572">1572</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mem de Sá was the third governor-general of Portuguese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>, serving from 1557 until his death in 1572. With <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuit</a> support he attacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> Antarctique in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guanabara-bay">Guanabara Bay</a> in 1560 and fought the Tamoio. His nephew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estacio-de-sa">Estácio de Sá</a> founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-janeiro">Rio de Janeiro</a> in 1565, and the French were finally driven out in 1567.</p></div>
